From 024b53b2688e042b468d361026b6fa6d76b40ada Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:52:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 54/57] reefamr: the gauges and probes of NHFLOW, FNPF, SFLOW
 read the finest grid

The printers of the column models read level 0, which under a patch holds the restriction of the
patch.  amr_grid_lookup.h gets amr_column_lookup (the finest patch of a rank at (x,y)) and
amr_point_owners (collective: the rank that writes a point of an output, the one with the finest
grid there; points on level 0 alone as before), amr_points (the grids of the points of an output).
reefamr::finest_point finds the finest local patch whose interior holds the point with the cells
within two of it interior or boundary values (not filled from another grid).  nhflow_amr,
fnpf_amr and sflow_amr implement the lookup, the printers take it after the setup of the
refinement: NHFLOW P 51, P 64, P 65; FNPF P 51, P 65; SFLOW P 51, P 63.  The lines and the run-up
stay on level 0.  With the placement (G 40) a point is written by the rank of its finest grid.

The states are unchanged; the WSF files of the cases with refinement and gauges change (the SFLOW
dam break: 3-10 times closer to the uniform fine run, validation/32).

